  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "While Kim notes down the different base plans possible, Soum pulls a lever from the control room, and Kim falls into a trapped cell! Has the JSA won the battle?\n\nUnfortunately for the JSA, Kim is a genius, so he has obviously easily escaped from his cell. However, he found that his cell is only one in a large underground network of cells. Now he needs to find a way to escape!\n\nOf course, since it is a prison, some of the cells are locked at all times. However, some prison guards are lazy and left the keys for a cell in another cell. Each key can only unlock one cell and each cell can only be unlocked by one key. If any cell does not have a corresponding key, it is unlocked.\n\nThe prison consists of NNN cells labelled 1 to NNN with cell 1 being Kim's starting position and cell NNN being the exit of the underground prison network. Furthermore, there are EEE bidirectional connections between cells. The iii-th connection takes Kim CiC_iCi​ seconds to pass through, and connects cells AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​. Kim takes no time to pick up a key when he reaches a cell containing a key, and takes no time to unlock a door with a key. Cells 1 and NNN never have any keys in them. Additionally, no two keys will ever be found in the same cell.\n\nCan you help Kim find the minimum time it would take him to go from cell 1 to cell NNN?\n\n###Input:\n\nThe first line of input contains 3 integers NNN, EEE and KKK denoting the number of cells, number of connections and the number of keys.\n\nThe following EEE lines contain 3 integers, AiA_iAi​, BiB_iBi​ and CiC_iCi​ showing that a connection exists between cell AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​ taking CiC_iCi​ time to traverse.\n\nThe following KKK lines contain 2 integers, LLL and UUU denoting that the key for cell UUU is located at cell LLL.\n\n###Output:\n\nPrint one number SSS which is the time from cell 1 to cell NNN. If this is not possible print -1.\n\nThe answer is guaranteed to fit into a 64 bit integer.\n\n###Subtasks\r\nFor all subtasks, 5≤N≤1000005 \\leq N \\leq 1000005≤N≤100000, 4≤E≤2000004 \\leq E \\leq 2000004≤E≤200000, 0≤K≤120 \\leq K \\leq 120≤K≤12. For all edges, 1≤A,B≤N1 \\leq A, B \\leq N1≤A,B≤N, 1≤C≤1091 \\leq C \\leq 10^91≤C≤109. All key nodes and lock nodes are distinct. No cell contains both a key and a lock, and no cell contains more than one key or more than one lock. In addition, cells 111 and NNN will never have a key or lock. Connections may connect a node to itself, and multiple connections may exist between two nodes.\n\nSubtask 1 [30 points]: N≤20000N \\leq 20000N≤20000, E≤100000E \\leq 100000E≤100000, K=0K = 0K=0\n\nSubtask 2 [30 points]: N≤10000N \\leq 10000N≤10000, E≤20000E \\leq 20000E≤20000, K≤6K \\leq 6K≤6\n\nSubtask 3 [40 points]: N≤100000N \\leq 100000N≤100000, E≤200000E \\leq 200000E≤200000, K≤12K \\leq 12K≤12\n\n###Sample Input:\n\n`5 4 1\r\n1 2 5\r\n2 3 7\r\n3 4 8\r\n4 5 2\r\n2 3\n`###Sample Output:\n\n`22\n`",
